Each claim row now has an amount box and a "Save amount" button next to the Edit button. `bin/e2e` passes all 4 tests in the spec.

The change is front-end only, in `src/main/frontend/features/claims/ClaimList.tsx`. The save sends the new amount to the same endpoint the claim editor uses (`PUT /api/sheets/{sheetId}/claims/{claimId}`), along with the claim's current date, note and corrects number, so those stay as they are. That means it follows exactly the editor's existing server rules:

- the amount may have at most two decimals, and a negative one must name the claim it corrects;
- only a DRAFT claim can be changed;
- it is refused while another user has the claim's editor open;
- it is refused when the claim's due-by date falls in a closed period;
- a viewer can't use it.

A successful save writes `CLAIM_EDITED` (plus any rollup lines) and refreshes the claims and people figures.

A refusal shows the row's `claim-error`. That error clears on your next action on the row, including typing in the amount box.

The amount box shows on every claim, not only drafts. The test tries it on an OPEN claim and expects the error, so the box has to be there. This matches the Edit button, which also shows on every claim.
